    "narrative": "For LawDog, the path to offensive production on this June 28th slate is headlined by our outfield core, with **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Daulton Varsho** (68.44) serving as the day's high-leverage anchors. **Taylor Ward** benefits from a premier matchup against Littell in a favorable park, and while the 30% rain risk is a nuisance, his position atop the order provides the volume we crave. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** is a priority start; he enjoys a massive boost from a dynamic platoon edge and the presence of a slow-moving pitcher on the mound, which significantly inflates his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our 5x5 scarcity strategy. **Jonathan Aranda** (70.46) also profiles as an elite play today, utilizing a robust 19% SP skill boost and an advantageous #2 spot in the lineup to maximize his run-scoring opportunities.\n\nThe optimizer faced a difficult internal deliberation regarding **Luis Arraez** on the bench. Despite his high floor, the combination of facing Chris Sale\u2019s elite repertoire and the negative platoon splits forced him to a 40.93 score, keeping him just outside the starting nine. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Dylan Beavers** (68.38); although he is a strong play thanks to the same park and pitcher benefits as **Taylor Ward**, the shared 30% weather risk across those slots could leave us vulnerable if the storms materialize. We are keeping a close eye on **Geraldo Perdomo** (44.11) and **Bryson Stott** (46.15) as well; both face tough, high-skill arms in Rasmussen and P\u00e9rez, respectively, and are strictly marginal starts intended only to maintain our plate appearance consistency while we prioritize our high-upside outfielders like **Lawrence Butler** (60.03), who is bolstered by helpful wind conditions today.",
